[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Italian Game: Evans Gambit"]
[ECO "C52"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "pawn-grab"]
[Themes "take-and-retreat,centre-fight"]
[Kind "gambit"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 { White offers a pawn to hit the bishop and open the centre quickly. } 4... Bxb4 { Take it. The pawn is real: if Black defends carefully, White's lead in development runs out. }
5. c3 { Attacks the bishop and prepares d4. } 5... Be7 { Retreats to a safe square. This is the simplest way to keep the extra pawn. }
6. d4 { White grabs the centre. } 6... Na5 { Attacks the bishop on c4. It is White's best attacking piece, and Black wants it traded or driven away. }
7. Be2 { The bishop retreats, because Nxc4 would cost White the pair of bishops. }
( 7. Nxe5 Nxc4 8. Nxc4 d5 { Hits the centre: Black gives the extra pawn back for a free game and safe king. } 9. exd5 Qxd5 10. Ne3 Qd8 )
7... exd4 { Swaps Black's e-pawn for White's d-pawn, opening lines for Black's pieces and leaving Black a pawn ahead. }
8. Qxd4 8... Nf6 { Develops a piece and attacks the e4 pawn. }
9. e5 9... Nc6 { Brings a knight back into play with an attack on the queen. } 10. Qh4 10... Nd5 { Saves the knight and guards the bishop on e7 from the queen on h4. Plan: Black is a pawn up, so castle, trade pieces and watch the squares around the king. } *
